```jython:import collections\nfrom pandas import DataFrame\n# Assuming you have a DataFrame df with 'lowest_price' and 'dish_name' columns
grouped = df.groupby('dish_name')['lowest_price'].mean()\ngrouped_sorted = grouped.sort_values(ascending=False)\npopular_dishes = grouped_sorted.head(10).index.tolist()\n# Add a new column 'times_appeared' to the DataFrame
df['times_appeared'] = df['dish_name'].apply(lambda x: collections.Counter(df['dish_name'])[x])\ndf_sorted = df.sort_values('times_appeared', ascending=False)\n# Select top 10 dishes based on 'times_appeared' column
top_dishes = df_sorted.head(10)['dish_name']\n# Calculate average price for the top 10 dishes
average_prices = grouped_sorted.loc[top_dishes].mean()```

